### Description

Modifying the position of the scene can cause misalignment of the SpotLight and SpotLightHelper positions

### Reproduction steps

If the scene is not at the origin, it will trigger an error

### Code

```js
// mesh
const plane = new THREE.Mesh(
  new THREE.PlaneGeometry(100, 100),
  new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: '#ccc' })
);
plane.rotation.x = -Math.PI / 2
plane.receiveShadow = true
scene.add(plane);

const flag = new THREE.Mesh(
  new THREE.BoxGeometry(1, 1, 1),
  new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 'red' })
);
flag.position.y = 10;
scene.add(flag);

// light
const spotLight = new THREE.SpotLight('#fff');
spotLight.castShadow = true;
spotLight.angle = Math.PI / 180 * 30
spotLight.intensity = 2
spotLight.distance = 20
spotLight.penumbra = 0.1
spotLight.decay = 0.1
const spotLightHelper = new THREE.SpotLightHelper(spotLight);
scene.add(spotLight, spotLightHelper);
spotLight.position.y = 10

// Trigger
scene.position.y = -2
```


