comments:
It should be possible to ensure the helper is _always_ positioned at the same point as the target light regardless of hierarchy position, no? You just need to transform the target lights world transformation in the local frame of the helpers parent.

I'd have to test and double check the math but this is roughly what we'd have to do and then I believe it would always work.

```js
const invMatrix = new Matrix4();
const localMatrix = new Matrix4();
const parent = light.parent;
const target = light.target;

// transform into the parents local frame
invMatrix
  .copy( parent.matrixWorld )
  .invert();

// transform the targets frame into the local frame
localMatrix
  .copy( target.matrixWorld )
  .premultiply( invMatrix )
  .decompose( helper.position, helper.quaternion, helper.scale );
```
